# Scope
Approved n356 implementation only in ciel-runtime-wt-work. Existing classic.Stop,
INSTRUCTIONS queue-selection edits, selection backend and approval logic retained.
No commit, push, install, remote access or actual CLI E2E performed.

# Implementation
- Display-only panel atom resets with conversation identity and session end.
- Progress excludes status=done; Queue lists roots only; Completed uses current
  snapshot status, never done/total equality, and exposes completed active rows.
- Whole band capped to min(10, viewport rows / 4, maxRows - 2), reserving native
  preview rows. Tiny widths/heights use Inspect Work; below two budget rows yields
  to native host. Native view retains downstream next(e) tree and pages its window.
- List and inspector controls page without Work mutations. Exact selected fields
  are fetched on demand; notes/evidence and long/wide titles remain page-accessible.
- root_index and completed_active snapshot summaries are bounded by MAX_NODES=600.
  root_index includes every root beyond the 20-entry queue preview, no notes,
  evidence or queued descendants. No persistence schema changes.

# Verified
- Isolated mod runner: strict validation success, 62 pass / 0 fail.
- Focused unittest discovery: tree, MCP tools, HTTP controller, statusline;
  93 pass. Environment cleared with env -i, temporary HOME/profile/config paths.
- git diff --check passed for edited code/test/type files.
- Evidence: evidence/mod-ui-tests.txt and evidence/python-ui-tests.txt.

# Limitations
The host test harness validates trees and exercises button handlers, not terminal
painting. Native engine refs, actual viewport clipping/focus and screenshot proof
remain the caller-owned n357 real CLI E2E. No claim of rendered screenshot proof.
The initial backend consumer sweep lacked HOME and failed; rerun with isolated
home directories passed. The final evidence file contains the successful run.
An attempted n356 done update used stale expected_version=0 and was rejected;
no Work state was changed by this implementation session.
